<dc:title>Capitol Reflecting Pool</dc:title>
<dc:description>&lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/82&quot;&gt;Pierre L&#039;Enfant&lt;/a&gt;&#039;s &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/168&quot;&gt;1791 plan&lt;/a&gt; for the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/393&quot;&gt;city of Washington&lt;/a&gt; first suggested a reflecting pool for the Capitol, but was never built. The &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/350&quot;&gt;1902 McMillian Commission&lt;/a&gt; design for the National Mall revived the idea, yet it still took until 1971 for the Reflecting Pool to be completed.</dc:description>
<dc:source>Architect of the Capitol. &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.aoc.gov/capitol-grounds/capitol-reflecting-pool&quot;&gt;View original&lt;/a&gt;.</dc:source>
